170
00:13:49,146 --> 00:13:51,813
Task one. Pause, drag the shaft angle,

171
00:13:51,833 --> 00:13:55,419
and find where the lever pulls the thread tightest,

172
00:13:55,439 --> 00:14:00,792
the moment the supply is zero. Then compare it with the eye's highest point.

173
00:14:01,192 --> 00:14:07,058
Task two. Set the cloth to 3 millimetres. Watch the whole demand curve rise,

174
00:14:07,078 --> 00:14:12,092
and when you do the lab, write down the indicators at this point.

175
00:14:12,492 --> 00:14:17,410
Then move only the thread guide, leaving the spring stroke,

176
00:14:17,430 --> 00:14:21,260
the link dimensions and the hook timing alone,

177
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:27,872
until all three criteria are met. Record the guide position and the indicators.

178
00:14:28,272 --> 00:14:32,317
Task three. Put the cloth and the guide back,

179
00:14:32,337 --> 00:14:36,472
then bring the catch earlier than 198 degrees,

180
00:14:36,492 --> 00:14:41,350
and watch how the extra thread round the case changes.

181
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:46,790
Then make it later than 214, and watch the minimum margin.

182
00:14:46,810 --> 00:14:52,810
Record both sets and check them against the example from the lecture.

183
00:14:53,210 --> 00:14:57,763
